From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rob Vogelaar <rob.vogelaar@libertyglobal.com>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 19:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] controller: synchronize profile on every agent radio

The current handler updates the AL node and persistent device after validating
the peer's Topology Response profile. Controller radio objects can still retain
the profile with which they happened to be created, causing valid Profile-2/3
metrics TLVs to be rejected.

Apply the negotiated profile to every controller radio belonging to the agent.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Rob Vogelaar <rob.vogelaar@libertyglobal.com>
---
 src/em/config/em_configuration.cpp | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/em/config/em_configuration.cpp b/src/em/config/em_configuration.cpp
--- a/src/em/config/em_configuration.cpp
+++ b/src/em/config/em_configuration.cpp
@@ -2515,6 +2515,16 @@ int em_configuration_t::handle_topology_response(unsigned char *buff, unsigned i
         al_em->set_peer_profile(m_peer_profile);
     }
     dm->m_device.m_device_info.profile = m_peer_profile;
+
+    // A radio can be created before the asynchronous device-model commit
+    // records the profile. Keep every runtime radio for this Agent in sync.
+    std::vector<em_t *> agent_radios;
+    get_mgr()->get_all_em_for_al_mac(src_al_mac, agent_radios);
+    for (auto *radio : agent_radios) {
+        if (radio != nullptr) {
+            radio->set_profile_type(m_peer_profile);
+        }
+    }
     if (em_msg_t(em_msg_type_topo_resp, m_peer_profile, buff, len).validate(errors) == 0) {
         em_printfout("topology response msg validation failed, ignoring message");
         return -1;
